    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee25042b_3ce1ef58",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/BuiltInCodeSnippetID.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-04T20:18:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment is going to cover some broader design thoughts around these snippets, and how they intersect the refactor I\u0027d been working on:\n\nHaving a block/snippet that provides the dst color is something that I had been thinking would useful for detangling the many different blend snippet IDs whose primary difference is how to wire up the src and dst children. If a blender is used as the last blend on the PaintParams, its dst can be the kDstColor block.\n\nHowever, I think it would be better to keep the DstColor block uniform-less and sampler-less so that it can be used independently of how the dst readback is implemented. It would also mean we can build the key and extract the rest of the paint uniforms up front (even within Device) and then later stick on the required values for dst readback. I think this could be handled in the DstColor snippet entry by leveraging the ShaderSnippet::Args object and making sure its dst variable referred to the value that would be set up by the outer SkSL template.\n\nRelated to this SkSL template, I don\u0027t know if having a kFinalBlend block is necessary. I can see that it acts as a single root to combine the paint\u0027s final blend and any coverage modulation that has to happen, but I don\u0027t see any reason why that specific logic can\u0027t just be part of the template SkSL that\u0027s directly appended in `ShaderInfo::toSkSL`.  This would shorten the PaintParamsKey and its root would just be the final blend block. It also helps keep the PaintParamsKey more independent from the RenderStep/Renderer.\n\nThe snippet generation system was set up to glue together SkSL sources from all the various `SkFoo` objects, but I don\u0027t think this final shader logic needs that level of indirection.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "db648177c1c766db7dc69e791ecc0e28e126a316",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f779224_ade517d5",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/BuiltInCodeSnippetID.h",
