        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:57:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This now does the actual dst read in a dst read block which is added to the beginning of a shader. But as mentioned in a later comment I\u0027m not sure this will work when trying to account for coverage, since we don\u0027t associate render steps with paint params when setting up shader snippet blocks.",
      "parentUuid": "ee25042b_3ce1ef58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "db648177c1c766db7dc69e791ecc0e28e126a316",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ee837da_8a92db35",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/BuiltInCodeSnippetID.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-04T20:18:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now all of these snippets directly modify the skgpu::BlendInfo that\u0027s associated with a ShaderInfo instead of generating additional SkSL. They also only really make sense as the root node since they should only come up as the final blend (or at least root in my proposed modification where the node that combines the blend output and coverage is not represented in the paint\u0027s tree).\n\nI\u0027m not exactly sure how this will need to change but it may just mean that the recorded skgpu::BlendInfo is set once by these snippets and then modified to account for coverage-as-alpha, etc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "db648177c1c766db7dc69e791ecc0e28e126a316",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
