    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c30af00e_37e4e714",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Caps.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-04T20:18:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO this doesn\u0027t fit my mental model for Caps. The DstReadRequirement is primarily defining *how* the dst value is available, which does seem like a relevant piece of info for Caps to provide.  But deciding whether or not a given paint needs the dst seems like it should be handled with the rest of the rendering logic.\n\nIn particular, Device has a static function `paint_depends_on_dst` that has very similar series of if-statements to the current impl of `getDstReadRequirement`.  Currently they have nuanced differences because `paint_depends_on_dst` returns true if the final color is affected by the dst color which is a broader mode than whether or not the shader needs access to the dst color in order to compute the final color. Device is also responsible for picking the Renderer, which determines if the coverage modulation has to happen, and that can modify or tweak any fixed-function blend or actually require the dst color in shader.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "db648177c1c766db7dc69e791ecc0e28e126a316",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
