    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc36074c_20b7c3ee",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ShaderCodeDictionary.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 460,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-04T20:18:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A big part of my refactor is that the preamble generation happens once up front and tracking of the `entryIndex` across children pretty much completely goes away, so it will mostly just clean up this code, assuming it stays as a snippet.\n\nI think I there are \"final blend\"s that we would need to handle, and maybe they are explicitly written out in the `toSkSL` function, or maybe we provide enough info to the PaintParams.toKey() function that we can record the final blend type in the key, even if some of its parameters (e.g. the dst color or the coverage value) are passed in explicitly from another source. I think we have:\n\n1. HW fixed-function blend based solely on the SkPaint\u0027s coefficient-based SkBlendMode, and there\u0027s no analytic coverage to fold in.\n2. As #1, but we have to fold an analytic coverage value into the shader\u0027s output color and possibly tweak the blend functions to produce the coverage-modulated blend result (e.g. dual-source blending).\n3. The dst color is available in shader *somehow* and we just need to call the blend functions and coverage modulation in SkSL",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 460,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 460,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "db648177c1c766db7dc69e791ecc0e28e126a316",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da495644_9e941efa",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ShaderCodeDictionary.cpp",
